# o1_key_stream
#
# donor      SHARK s1_batch_check_stream (s3_key_stream: same mechanism on key material).
# mechanism  stream a file upstream reads whole.
# basis      o0_default peak 23,825,532 kB (party 3, client); 94.3% one object:
#            heap:readFile(std::__cxx11::basic_string<...>), 22,463,872 kB.
# source     bertbenchmark.cpp calls llama->init(ip, true); memBuf = true -> _kBuf = readFile("server.dat")
#            (whole key file, one allocation). MemBuf::read(int) (comms.h:175) returns pointers into
#            it, so the buffer lives for the whole run.
# lever      upstream default memBuf = false (llama_base.h:89): Dealer over FileBuf (comms.h:96),
#            std::fstream::read of the same bytes in the same order into the caller's buffer.
#            Key material identical; residency changes.
# gate       T1s structural (all bytes at SocketBuf::read); reproduced byte-for-byte over four
#            baseline runs, moves under structural changes (off-path-runs/p_wire, p_disc; affine in depth).
# cost       memory free by construction; runtime decided by the wall (small reads, network filesystem).
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: readFile(std::__cxx11::basic_string<char, std::char_traits<char>, std::allocator<char> >)
